\begin{proof}[Proof of \cref{lm: convex EZ}]

		First of all, let us define $G_k^i := \left( \sum_{j = \tau^k_i}^{k-1}  \gamma_j d_{ij} \right)$ and $Z_k^i :=\left( \sum_{j = \tau^k_i}^{k-1}  \gamma_j d_{ij} \right)^2$ for $i \in [n]$, and also $G_k :=\sum_{i=1}^n G_k^i$ and $Z_k :=\sum_{i=1}^n Z_k^i$. Notice in $G_k^i$ and $Z_k^i$ that the randomness lies only in $\tau_i^k$, which in turn depends on the update sets $\calB_0, \calB_1,\dots,\calB_k$. 

